.SH stdio transport
\f[B]When to use:\f[R] Testing, CI/CD pipelines, sandboxed environments
where socket creation is restricted, or when you want a self\-contained
client\-server pair with no external socket file.
.PP
\f[B]How it works:\f[R] The client launches
\f[CR]bash\-server \-\-stdio\f[R] as a child process and communicates
over the child\(cqs stdin (client writes) and stdout (client reads).
The server runs in single\-session mode with no socket file.
.PP
The client manages the subprocess lifecycle: spawning at connect time,
and terminating (or waiting for exit) at close time.
.PP
\f[B]Connection examples:\f[R]
.PP
Python:
.IP
.EX
client = \f[B]await\f[R] BashClient.connect_stdio(\(dqbash\-server\(dq, \(dq\-\-stdio\(dq)

\f[I]# With additional arguments\f[R]
client = \f[B]await\f[R] BashClient.connect_stdio(
    \(dqbash\-server\(dq, \(dq\-\-stdio\(dq, \(dq\-\-login\(dq, \(dq\-\-init\(dq, \(dqsetup.sh\(dq
)
.EE
.PP
TypeScript:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] client = \f[B]await\f[R] BashClient.connectStdio(\(dqbash\-server\(dq, \(dq\-\-stdio\(dq);

\f[I]// With additional arguments\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] client = \f[B]await\f[R] BashClient.connectStdio(
    \(dqbash\-server\(dq, \(dq\-\-stdio\(dq, \(dq\-\-login\(dq
);
.EE
.PP
C:
.IP
.EX
const char *argv[] = {\(dqbash\-server\(dq, \(dq\-\-stdio\(dq, NULL};
bc_client_t *c = bc_connect_stdio(argv);

\f[I]/* With additional arguments */\f[R]
const char *argv2[] = {\(dqbash\-server\(dq, \(dq\-\-stdio\(dq, \(dq\-\-login\(dq, NULL};
bc_client_t *c2 = bc_connect_stdio(argv2);
.EE
.PP
Java:
.IP
.EX
BashClient client = BashClient.connectStdio(\(dqbash\-server\(dq, \(dq\-\-stdio\(dq);

\f[I]// With additional arguments\f[R]
BashClient client = BashClient.connectStdio(
    \(dqbash\-server\(dq, \(dq\-\-stdio\(dq, \(dq\-\-login\(dq
);
.EE
.PP
\f[B]Authentication in stdio mode:\f[R] The server prints the
authentication token to stderr when started in \f[CR]\-\-stdio\f[R]
mode.
The client can capture this from the subprocess stderr stream.
Alternatively, use \f[CR]\-\-token\f[R] to specify a known token, or
\f[CR]\-\-auth\-fd\f[R] to deliver the token over a separate file
descriptor.
.PP
\f[B]Security:\f[R] The subprocess runs as the same user.
stdin/stdout are private to the parent\-child pair.
No network or filesystem exposure.
This is the most isolated transport mode.
.PP
